    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nAny number raised to the power of zero is equal to [MATH: 1.] For example,\n[MATH: 2^0 = 1 \\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad (-55)^0=1.]\n\nContent:\nTo understand why, let's try to convince ourselves that [MATH: 2^0 = 1.] First, we write down a table containing all of the powers of [MATH: 2]:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 2^{4}|= 16; 2^{3}|= 8; 2^{2}|= 4; 2^{1}|= 2; 2^{0}|= \u25fb?]\n\nContent:\nAs we go down the list, the number in blue is divided by [MATH: 2] each time. Following this pattern, we must have\n[MATH: 2^{\\color{red}{0}} = {\\color{blue}{2}}\\div 2 = 1.]\n\nContent:\nIt doesn't matter whether the number is positive or negative, a fraction or a decimal, big or small. Raising any non-zero number to the power of zero always gives [MATH: 1.]\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Raising a Natural Number to the Power of Zero\n\nExample Prompt:\nWhat is [MATH: 9^0?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nAny number raised to the power of zero is equal to [MATH: 1.] So,\n[MATH: 9^0=1.]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 12^{0} =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 6]\nb. [MATH: 0]\nc. [MATH: 1]\nd. [MATH: 12]\ne. Undefined\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\nSimplify [MATH: 2^{0}.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 0]\nb. [MATH: 1]\nc. [MATH: 2]\nd. Undefined.\ne. [MATH: \u2212 1]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Example: Raising a Negative Integer to the Power of Zero\n\nExample Prompt:\nCalculate the value of [MATH: (-32\\,000)^0.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nAny number raised to the power of zero is equal to [MATH: 1.] So,\n[MATH: (-32\\,000)^0=1.]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\nWhat is the value of [MATH: \u2212 2520] raised to the power [MATH: 0?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 1]\nb. [MATH: 0]\nc. [MATH: 2520]\nd. [MATH: 25200]\ne. [MATH: 252]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\nSimplify [MATH: (\u2212 1)^{0}.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 0]\nb. [MATH: 1]\nc. [MATH: \u2212 1]\nd. [MATH: 2]\ne. Undefined.\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Example: Raising a Rational Number to the Power of Zero\n\nExample Prompt:\nWhat is the value of [MATH: \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^0?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nAny number raised to the power of zero is equal to [MATH: 1.] So,\n[MATH: \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^0=1.]\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (\u2212 (100)/(124))^{0} =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (100)/(124)]\nb. [MATH: 1]\nc. [MATH: \u2212 1]\nd. [MATH: 0]\ne. [MATH: \u2212 (100)/(124)]\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\nCalculate the value of [MATH: ((9)/(8))^{0}.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 1(1)/(8)]\nb. [MATH: \u2212 1]\nc. [MATH: 1]\nd. [MATH: (9)/(8)]\ne. [MATH: 0]\n\n---\n\nItem 11 \u2014 Example: Raising a Decimal Number to the Power of Zero\n\nExample Prompt:\nFind the value of [MATH: (-0.693)^0.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nAny number raised to the power of zero is equal to [MATH: 1.] So,\n[MATH: (-0.693)^0=1.]\n\n---\n\nItem 12 \u2014 Question 7\n\nPrompt:\nFind the value of [MATH: (9.2596)^{0}.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 92.596]\nb. [MATH: 1]\nc. [MATH: 9.2596]\nd. [MATH: 0]\ne. [MATH: 0.92596]\n\n---\n\nItem 13 \u2014 Question 8\n\nPrompt:\nCalculate [MATH: (3.3196)^{0}.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 3.3196]\nb. [MATH: 0.33196]\nc. [MATH: 1]\nd. [MATH: 0]\ne. [MATH: 33.196]"
